    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required that a created owner return a `displayName` formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName`. Following the project's OfficeFloor/DTO conventions (DTOs are generated from the OpenAPI schema; entity\u2192DTO conversion goes through the MapStruct `OwnerMapper`), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct mapping on `toOwnerDto(Owner)` that computes it from the stored names:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"displayName\", expression = \"java(owner.getLastName() + \\\", \\\" + owner.getFirstName())\")\n   ```\n\nBecause both the create (`RespondWithOwnerCreated`) and fetch (`RespondWithOwner`) pipelines share `toOwnerDto`, `displayName` is populated consistently. The acceptance test `coreComputesDisplayName` (create \u2192 GET \u2192 assert `$.displayName == \"LastName, John\"`) passes, and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with 0 failures.",
